WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.240
What do you like best or least about
your job? The editors of AEI's

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.110
Political Report have been exploring
workers answers. They find that most

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.430
workers are highly satisfied with most
aspects of their jobs. In a Gallup poll,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.420
more than nine in ten employed people
said they were completely or somewhat

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.109
satisfied with the safety of their
workplace, their co-workers, and the

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:28.920
flexibility of their hours. Around 80
percent are satisfied with the amount of

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.759
work required of them, the recognition
they get on the job, and the amount of

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.680
vacation time they get. 81 percent are
even satisfied with their boss or

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.059
supervisor. In the poll, workers were
least satisfied about their health and

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:46.710
retirement benefits and on-the-job
stress, but even in these areas more than

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:51.149
two-thirds said they were satisfied.
Americans' views about the economy, their

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.280
jobs, and their futures are more positive
now than they have been in a long time.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.660
In a new Bloomberg poll, nearly six in ten
said that they were moving closer to

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.590
their hopes for their careers and
finances. That's good news on Labor Day.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:11.640
To learn more about my take on American
attitudes toward work, see the new issue

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.290
of AEI's Political Report. Also, let us
know what other topics you want our

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.490
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to subscribe for more research and

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.509
videos from AEI.

